{
 "hypothesis": "H42-1 hanging-wall conditional intensity (HWCI) \u2014 P(new fault | distance, topographically signed side, strike alignment to the nearest visible trace, local scarp evidence), fitted by fault-component hide-and-recover.",
 "mechanism": "Synthetic/antithetic hanging-wall splays and basinward-stepping piedmont scarps form on the down-thrown side of mapped normal faults at 0.3-3 km; the side is signed by smoothed det_elev relative to the nearest visible trace (no dip attribute needed).",
 "non_fault_mimic": "Pluvial Lake Lahontan shorelines and fan-toe/terrace risers: level, scarp-like steps that lie on the same (basinward) side the hypothesis favours; not separable without absolute elevation.",
